From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 16:20:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a5xx: don't preempt while per-process pagetables are
 on

Preemption and per-process pagetables are mutually exclusive on a5xx,
and this tree can enable both: msm8998 is denylisted from
IO_PGTABLE_QUIRK_ARM_TTBR1 upstream by
commit a0bee0086c47 ("iommu/arm-smmu-qcom: Skip the TTBR1 quirk for
MSM8998 and SDM630"), and that denylist is commented out in our
drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c.

a5xx_preempt_hw_init() programs CP_CONTEXT_SWITCH_SMMU_INFO = 0 -- "we
aren't switching pagetables" -- because upstream a5xx has no
per-process pagetables and its preemption code may assume a single
TTBR0 across every ring. With the denylist bypassed,
a5xx_set_pagetable() emits a CP_SMMU_TABLE_UPDATE per submit whenever
a private vm is in use. A ring restored by preemption resumes mid-ring
without replaying that packet, and the preemption record carries no
SMMU info to restore it, so it runs against whichever TTBR0 the ring
it preempted away from happened to leave installed.

Measured on taimen. Even with the upstream preemption fixes in place,
opening any GL application strands a submit -- the CP stops a submit
short (rb0 rptr 94 / wptr 131, fence 205/206) and the compositor
blocks forever in DRM_IOCTL_MSM_WAIT_FENCE, which presents as "the
screen froze and touch is dead" while input and the rest of the
system stay healthy. Worse, the hangcheck that does eventually fire
runs the crashdumper, which faults, so recovery fails with -EINVAL and
takes the GPU down for good.

With preemption off the same phosh session -- Settings, gedit, the
on-screen keyboard -- is fully usable, with no hangchecks, no faults
and no errors logged.

This mirrors that upstream fix from the other side: upstream
disables the pagetables, we disable the preemption. Restoring that
denylist instead was tried here and regressed badly -- it faulted
sooner and the greeter never started -- so preemption is the cheaper
half to give up.

Add the a5xx_enable_preemption module parameter (a5xx_gpu_init()
drops nr_rings to 1 when it's false, and a5xx_preempt_init() already
no-ops for nr_rings <= 1) so the configuration stays reachable for
whoever teaches the preemption record to carry SMMU info, and default
it to false rather than ripping preemption out entirely.

Named a5xx_enable_preemption, not enable_preemption: 6.18 already has
a global, A7xx-only "enable_preemption" tri-state int param in
adreno_device.c (drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c:19-21,
consumed via extern in a6xx_gpu.c). A second module_param() of the
same name in the same module (msm.ko) would register a second
"enable_preemption" entry under the same sysfs parameters directory --
different type, different chip, same name -- which is exactly the kind
of collision module parameters aren't allowed to have. a5xx and a7xx
preemption are unrelated code paths gated on different bugs, so giving
this one its own name is both the fix and the more upstreamable shape:
it doesn't presume to redefine what "enable_preemption" means
tree-wide.

This folds in what taimen-v6.0 carried as two commits (63a3483177f6,
which first added the parameter defaulted to true, and 01d684dc2676,
which flipped the default to false once the per-process-pagetable
interaction was root-caused) into one, since 6.18's a5xx_gpu_init()
already carries its own nr_rings variable and shipping the parameter
pre-broken for even one commit isn't useful here.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c | 45 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 45 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c
index adf1350e77c1..c32ddbd69793 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 #include <linux/types.h>
 #include <linux/cpumask.h>
 #include <linux/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.h>
+#include <linux/moduleparam.h>
 #include <linux/pm_opp.h>
 #include <linux/nvmem-consumer.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
@@ -16,6 +17,47 @@
 extern bool hang_debug;
 static void a5xx_dump(struct msm_gpu *gpu);
 
+/*
+ * Preemption and per-process pagetables are mutually exclusive on a5xx, and
+ * this tree enables both -- so preemption is off by default.
+ *
+ * a5xx_preempt_hw_init() programs CP_CONTEXT_SWITCH_SMMU_INFO = 0, i.e. "we
+ * aren't switching pagetables". Upstream a5xx has no per-process pagetables,
+ * so its preemption code may assume a single TTBR0 across every ring. Here,
+ * the msm8998 denylist in qcom_adreno_can_do_ttbr1() (drivers/iommu/arm/
+ * arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c) is commented out, so IO_PGTABLE_QUIRK_ARM_TTBR1
+ * is available and a5xx_set_pagetable() emits a CP_SMMU_TABLE_UPDATE per
+ * submit whenever a private (per-process) vm is in use. A ring restored by
+ * preemption resumes mid-ring without replaying that packet, and the
+ * preemption record carries no SMMU info to restore it -- so it runs against
+ * whichever TTBR0 the ring it preempted away from happened to leave
+ * installed.
+ *
+ * Measured 2026-07-27. With preemption on, opening any GL app strands a
+ * submit: the CP stops a submit short (rb0 rptr 94 / wptr 131, fence
+ * 205/206) and the compositor blocks forever in DRM_IOCTL_MSM_WAIT_FENCE.
+ * With preemption off the same phosh session -- Settings, gedit, on-screen
+ * keyboard -- is fully usable.
+ *
+ * That is upstream a0bee0086c47 ("Skip the TTBR1 quirk for MSM8998 and
+ * SDM630", "Adreno 5xx doesn't have separate pagetables support") reached
+ * from the other side: it disables the pagetables, we disable the
+ * preemption. Restoring that denylist instead was tried and regressed
+ * badly, so this is the cheaper half to give up. Re-enabling preemption
+ * requires teaching the preemption record to carry SMMU info first.
+ *
+ * Named a5xx_enable_preemption rather than enable_preemption: 6.18 already
+ * has a global "enable_preemption" module param in adreno_device.c that is
+ * A7xx-only (tri-state int: 1=on, 0=off, -1=auto). Reusing that name here
+ * would register two "enable_preemption" kernel parameters for the msm
+ * module -- different types, different chips, same sysfs node -- so this
+ * gets its own name instead of colliding with it.
+ */
+static bool a5xx_enable_preemption;
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(a5xx_enable_preemption,
+		 "Enable preemption (A5XX only; broken while per-process pagetables are on)");
+module_param(a5xx_enable_preemption, bool, 0600);
+
 #define GPU_PAS_ID 13
 
 static void update_shadow_rptr(struct msm_gpu *gpu, struct msm_ringbuffer *ring)
@@ -1784,6 +1826,9 @@ struct msm_gpu *a5xx_gpu_init(struct drm_device *dev)
 	if (config->info->revn == 510)
 		nr_rings = 1;
 
+	if (!a5xx_enable_preemption)
+		nr_rings = 1;
+
 	ret = adreno_gpu_init(dev, pdev, adreno_gpu, &funcs, nr_rings);
 	if (ret) {
 		a5xx_destroy(&(a5xx_gpu->base.base));
